L0203: Declaration rejected by logical checking

The declaration violates a condition needed for checked definitions, such as positivity of recursive logical data, a valid dependency order, or a callable declaration body. Read the specific cause in the primary message. Negative recursive payloads cannot be repaired by adding an unchecked assertion.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/logical_mutual_negative_recursion.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
#[derive(Logical)]
enum Left { Next(logic Fn(Right) -> Int) }
#[derive(Logical)]
enum Right { Next(Left) }
```

Language, as built: [1.25:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.25:2).
